allation/web)[Webflow](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/installation/webflow)\n174-\n175-Where to use\n176-\n177-[PostHog Web](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/surfaces/web-app)\n178-\n--\n192-\n193-[](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog.com/blob/master/contents/docs/session-replay/installation/flutter.mdx)\n194-\n195-Copy page\n196-\n197:# Flutter Session Replay installation\n198-\n199-#### Contents\n200-\n201-*   Control recording programmatically\n202-\n203-1.    1   ## Install the package\n204-\n205:Required  Add the PostHog Flutter SDK to your `pubspec.yaml`: pubspec.yaml  PostHog AI    ```yaml\n206-posthog_flutter: ^5.24.0\n207:```       **SDK version** Session replay requires PostHog Flutter SDK version 4.7.0 or higher. We recommend always using the latest version.     \n208-2.    2   ## Disable auto-init for Android\n209-\n210-Required  For session replay, you need to use manual initialization. Add this to your `AndroidManifest.xml` to disable auto-init: android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml  PostHog AI    ```xml\n211-<application>    <activity>        [...]    </activity>    <meta-data android:name=\"com.posthog.posthog.AUTO_INIT\" android:value=\"false\" /></application>\n212-```      Update the minimum Android SDK version to **21** in `android/app/build.gradle`: android/app/build.gradle  PostHog AI    ```groovy\n--\n219-```      Update the minimum platform version to iOS 13.0 in your `Podfile`: Podfile  PostHog AI    ```ruby\n220-platform :ios, '13.0'# rest of your config\n221-```        \n222-4.    4   ## Enable session recordings in project settings\n223-\n224:Required  Go to your PostHog [Project Settings](https://us.posthog.com/settings/project-replay) and enable **Record user sessions**. Session recordings will not work without this setting enabled. If you're using Flutter Web, also enable the **Canvas capture** setting. This is required as Flutter renders your app using a browser canvas element.   \n225-5.    5   ## Initialize PostHog with session replay\n226-\n227-Required  Initialize PostHog in your `main.dart` with session replay enabled. Here are all the available options: main.dart  PostHog AI    ```dart\n228-import 'package:flutter/material.dart';import 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n229:Future<void> main() async {  WidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();\n230-  final config = PostHogConfig('<ph_project_token>');  config.host = 'https://us.i.posthog.com';  config.debug = true;  config.captureApplicationLifecycleEvents = true;\n231:  // Enable session recording. Requires enabling in your project settings as well.  // Default is false.  config.sessionReplay = true;\n232:  // Enable masking of all text and text input fields. Default is true.  config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllTexts = false;\n233:  // Enable masking of all images. Default is true.  config.sessionReplayConfig.maskAllImages = false;\n234:  // Throttling delay used to reduce the number of snapshots captured. Default is 1s.  config.sessionReplayConfig.throttleDelay = const Duration(milliseconds: 1000);\n235-  await Posthog().setup(config);  runApp(MyApp());}\n236:```      For more configuration options, see the [Flutter session replay docs](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/installation?tab=Flutter).   \n237-6.    6   \n238-\n239:## Wrap your app with PostHogWidget\n240-\n241-Required  \n242-\n243:For Session Replay to work, wrap your app with `PostHogWidget` and add the `PosthogObserver`: \n244-\n245-    *   MaterialApp \n246-    *   go_router \n247-\n248-MyApp.dart\n249-\n250-PostHog AI\n251-\n252-```dart\n253-import 'package:flutter/material.dart';import 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n254:class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {  @override  Widget build(BuildContext context) {    return PostHogWidget(      child: MaterialApp(        navigatorObservers: [PosthogObserver()],        title: 'My App',        home: const HomeScreen(),      ),    );  }}\n255-```\n256-\n257-MyApp.dart\n258-\n259-PostHog AI\n260-\n261-```dart\n262-import 'package:flutter/material.dart';import 'package:go_router/go_router.dart';import 'package:posthog_flutter/posthog_flutter.dart';\n263:final GoRouter _router = GoRouter(  observers: [PosthogObserver()],  routes: [    GoRoute(      name: 'home',  // Name your routes for proper screen tracking      path: '/',      builder: (context, state) => const HomeScreen(),    ),  ],);\n264:class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {  @override  Widget build(BuildContext context) {    return PostHogWidget(      child: MaterialApp.router(        routerConfig: _router,        title: 'My App',      ),    );  }}\n265-```\n266-\n267-7.    7   ## Watch session recordings\n268-\n269-Recommended  Visit your site or app and interact with it for at least 10 seconds to generate a recording. Navigate between pages, click buttons, and fill out forms to capture meaningful interactions.\n--\n281-| [Console log recording](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/console-log-recording) | How to capture console logs in recordings |\n282-| [More tutorials](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/tutorials) | Other real-world examples and use cases |       \n283-\n284-## Control recording programmatically\n285-\n286:> Requires PostHog Flutter SDK version >= [5.14.0](https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-flutter/releases/5.14.0). Available on iOS, Android, and Web.\n287-\n288:Setting `config.sessionReplay = false` in your PostHog configuration will prevent PostHog from automatically starting session recordings on SDK setup.\n289-\n290-You can manually control when to start and stop session recordings using the following methods:\n291-\n292-*   `startSessionRecording({bool resumeCurrent = true})`\n293-    *   Set **resumeCurrent** to `true` to resume a previous session recording (default).\n--\n319-  @override  Widget build(BuildContext context) {    return const PinKeypad();  }}\n320-```\n321-\n322-`startSessionRecording()` resumes the current session by default, so the replay continues as one recording with the keypad left out. The `isSessionReplayActive()` check matters: on iOS, `startSessionRecording()` installs the replay integration if it isn't there yet, so an app that wasn't recording would start when the screen closes. Only resuming when the screen found recording active keeps that from happening.\n323-\n324:If you want taps left out of every recording rather than one screen's, set `sessionReplayConfig.captureTouches = false` before `setup()` instead (SDK >= 5.41.0); see [privacy controls](https://posthog.com/docs/session-replay/privacy).\n325-\n326-#### Record or ignore specific screens\n327-\n328-You can combine these methods with your navigation to record only certain screens, or to pause recording on sensitive ones. For example, using a `NavigatorObserver`, stop recording on a sensitive route and resume otherwise:\n329-\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
